call.raw_text:
{
  "workers": [
    {
      "worker": 1,
      "brief": "Read rows 1‑10 of the ledger (the rate table). Build a map of rate_code → unit_rate. No underpayment or duplicate checks are needed here. Return the completed map.",
      "ranges": [[1, 10]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 2,
      "brief": "You have rows 11‑40 (line items). Using the rate‑code map supplied by Worker 1, determine the unit rate for each line (use the line’s own unit_rate if present, otherwise look up its rate_code). Compute amount_owed = qty × unit_rate. If paid < amount_owed, record the line as UNDERPAID with its shortfall = amount_owed – paid (rounded to two decimals). Also record every claim_id you encounter and how many times it appears in your rows. Return two lists: (a) underpaid lines with row number, claim_id, shortfall; (b) claim_id counts.",
      "ranges": [[11, 40]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 3,
      "brief": "You have rows 41‑55 (line items). Perform the same analysis as Worker 2: compute underpaid lines and shortfalls, and tally claim_id occurrences in your rows. Return underpaid lines and claim_id counts.",
      "ranges": [[41, 55]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 4,
      "brief": "You have rows 56‑70 (line items). Perform the same analysis as Worker 2: compute underpaid lines and shortfalls, and tally claim_id occurrences in your rows. Return underpaid lines and claim_id counts.",
      "ranges": [[56, 70]]
    }
  ]
}

call.prompt:
You are auditing a remittance ledger with two sections. The rate table lists rate codes and their unit rates. Each line item is one billed service; it gives either its own unit_rate or a rate_code whose unit rate is in the rate table. The amount owed for a line is qty x unit rate. A line is UNDERPAID when paid is less than the amount owed; its shortfall is (amount owed) - paid, in currency units with two decimals. Lines paid exactly, or overpaid, are not underpayments and must not be reported as underpaid. A claim is DUPLICATED when the same claim_id appears on more than one line item (billed more than once). Find every underpaid line and every duplicated claim.

4 workers each checked part of the ledger. You do not see the ledger. Their reports:
Worker 1: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}
Worker 2: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}
Worker 3: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "RX-MZ572", "shortfall": 622.85}, {"line_id": "RX-C9TVB", "shortfall": 304.42}], "duplicates": [{"line_ids": ["RX-95H9X", "RX-B7SN9"]}]}
Worker 4: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}

Produce the final report.
Do not show your working or any explanation. Reply with only a JSON object: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "<line_id>", "shortfall": <amount with two decimals>}], "duplicates": [{"line_ids": ["<line_id>", "<line_id>"]}]}. List only lines whose shortfall is greater than 0. Use empty lists if there are none.
